# {{projectName}}

Welcome! **{{projectName}}** is a cross-platform desktop application built
with [Tauri 2](https://tauri.app): a React + Ant Design frontend rendered in
the system webview, driven by a Rust backend.

## Getting started

### One-time machine setup

1. **Registry auth** — the `dude` toolchain is published to GitHub Packages:

   ```bash
   export GITHUB_TOKEN=<personal access token with read:packages>
   ```

2. **Rust toolchain** — install from [rustup.rs](https://rustup.rs), then
   verify everything with:

   ```bash
   dude doctor
   ```

   On macOS you also need the Xcode Command Line Tools
   (`xcode-select --install`); on Linux, the webkit2gtk development packages —
   see the [Tauri prerequisites](https://tauri.app/start/prerequisites/).

### Run the app

```bash
pnpm install
dude dev
```

`dude dev` starts Vite on port 1420 and launches the desktop window; both the
frontend and the Rust backend hot-reload on change.

### Everyday loop

```bash
dude lint      # structural conventions (FE + Rust/Tauri)
dude test      # cargo test
dude review    # lint + ESLint + tsc + clippy
dude build     # distributable installers under src-tauri/target/
```

